\subsection{When is a survey completed?}

All summary modules must agree on what it means for a survey to be
completed, so we define completion once.
The evidence of completion is a date: a survey the student submitted has
[[submitted_at]], and one a teacher marked manually has [[graded_at]].
The grade plays no part, for the reason in the introduction.
Accepting [[None]] lets call sites map a missing submission
([[ResourceDoesNotExist]]) to \enquote{not completed} without duplicating
the rule.
<<functions>>=
def survey_completed(submission):
  """True iff the submission shows the survey was completed.

  Pass None (no submission exists) for not completed.
  """
  if submission is None:
    return False
  return bool(submission.submitted_at or submission.graded_at)
@

A survey counts as completed with either date, and as uncompleted with
neither date, even if it carries a grade---or with no submission at all.
<<test functions>>=
def test_survey_completed_by_submission_date(grading_objects):
  assert survey_completed(grading_objects.submission(
    "100", submitted_at="2026-07-01T10:00:00Z"))


def test_survey_completed_by_grading_date(grading_objects):
  assert survey_completed(grading_objects.submission(
    None, graded_at="2026-07-01T10:00:00Z"))


def test_survey_without_dates_not_completed(grading_objects):
  assert not survey_completed(grading_objects.submission(None))
  assert not survey_completed(grading_objects.submission("100"))


def test_missing_submission_not_completed():
  assert not survey_completed(None)
