\subsection{Reporting uncompleted surveys}

For [[--missing]], surveys follow the same rule in every module, whatever the
module does with the graded assignments: each uncompleted survey is missing,
and it is missing regardless of the student's grades, since completing it is
mandatory even for a student who passed everything else.
So the modules split the group in two, report the surveys here and handle
the rest by their own policy.
<<functions>>=
def split_surveys(assignments_list):
  """Return (surveys, others), each in the order of assignments_list."""
  surveys = []
  others = []
  for assignment in assignments_list:
    if is_survey(assignment):
      surveys.append(assignment)
    else:
      others.append(assignment)
  return surveys, others
@

The survey report applies the [[optional_assignments]] patterns itself,
because the surveys never reach the shared implementation in
[[canvaslms.cli.results]] that would otherwise apply them.
Its reason string is the same in every module, so the [[--missing]] output
reads the same whichever module computed it.
<<constants>>=
SURVEY_MISSING_REASON = "mandatory survey not completed"
<<functions>>=
def missing_surveys(surveys, users_list, optional_assignments=None):
  """Yield (user, survey, reason) for every survey a user hasn't completed.

  Surveys whose name matches a regex in optional_assignments are skipped.
  """
  for user in users_list:
    for assignment in surveys:
      if optional_assignments:
        if any(re.search(optional, assignment.name)
               for optional in optional_assignments):
          continue

      try:
        submission = assignment.get_submission(user)
      except ResourceDoesNotExist:
        submission = None

      if not survey_completed(submission):
        yield user, assignment, SURVEY_MISSING_REASON
@

Let's verify that a completed survey is never reported, that both kinds of
uncompleted survey are, and that an optional survey is not demanded.
<<test functions>>=
def test_split_surveys_keeps_order(grading_objects):
  survey = grading_objects.survey()
  lab = grading_objects.graded()
  feedback = grading_objects.points()

  assert split_surveys([lab, survey, feedback]) == ([survey], [lab, feedback])


def test_missing_surveys_reports_only_uncompleted(grading_objects):
  done = grading_objects.survey(grading_objects.submission(
    "100", submitted_at="2026-07-01T10:00:00Z"))
  dateless = grading_objects.survey(grading_objects.submission(None))
  absent = grading_objects.survey(None)
  user = grading_objects.user()

  rows = list(missing_surveys([done, dateless, absent], [user]))

  assert [(row[1], row[2]) for row in rows] == [
    (dateless, SURVEY_MISSING_REASON), (absent, SURVEY_MISSING_REASON)]


def test_optional_survey_not_reported(grading_objects):
  survey = grading_objects.survey(None, name="Optional survey")

  rows = list(missing_surveys([survey], [grading_objects.user()],
                              optional_assignments=["Optional"]))

  assert rows == []
